const POOLS := {
	"vera": {
		"greet": ["Well, look who wandered back into my little shop of hope, sugar, and you're just in time, because I've been saving a charm for someone with your exact level of bad judgment.", "Sit, sugar. The cards are warm, the incense is legal in most states, and I'm about to sell you hope at a markup you'll describe as a personal growth experience.", "Back for charms? Of course you are. Nobody visits me for my conversation, they visit because I'm the only one in this building who sells optimism without asking for their soul first.", "I was just telling the crystal ball about you, and it asked if you were the one who keeps paying full price for hope, and I said yes, that's him, he's my college fund."],
		"farewell": ["Go on, sugar, climb. And if the House eats you, do try to die near my shop, because the funeral crowd buys a lot of candles.", "Come back soon, and bring your wallet, because my charms work wonderfully, right up until the exact moment they stop, and I do not offer refunds for stopping.", "Climb safe, sugar. I mean it. You're my best customer, and dead customers just leave bad reviews in a language I can't read.", "Walk in the light, Rico, and if you can't find any, walk toward the sound of my cash register, it's the only thing around here that never lies."],
		"rich": ["Look at that wallet, sugar, it's so heavy it's practically begging me to relieve it, and I'm a woman who has always been kind to the needy.", "All that money and you came to see me? Darling, that's either wisdom or a cry for help, and honestly both of them pay the same.", "You're glowing, sugar, and I can't tell if that's wealth or a medical situation, so I'll sell you a charm for each and we'll see who's right.", "Rich suits you, Rico, and I mean that as a threat, because rich people buy the expensive charms, the ones that come with a little velvet bag and zero guarantees."],
		"broke": ["Empty pockets, sugar? That's fine, I deal in hope, and hope is the only thing I sell that costs nothing to make, so naturally I charge the most for it.", "Aw, you're broke. Sit, look at the charms, looking is free, touching is a felony, and I'll pretend I don't see how long you've been staring at the lucky rabbit foot.", "You're not broke, sugar, you're pre-rich, it's a whole market segment, and I just happen to sell charms that work specifically on people who are pre-rich and almost out of options.", "Come back when you've robbed someone, preferably someone with insurance, and I'll sell you a charm that makes the police feel a sudden, unexplainable sleepiness."],
		"ugly": ["Sugar, what are you wearing, and should I be calling someone, because that outfit has the exact look of a hostage situation where the hostage lost.", "That outfit is a curse, darling, and I'd know, because I sell curses, and mine at least have the decency to come in a nice box.", "Even the slot machines looked away when you walked in, and sugar, they have no eyes, they just have the instinct to avoid it.", "Go see Silas, honey, he'll have a stroke when he sees that, and I'll sell tickets, front row, with a charm for fainting included."],
		"sharp": ["Now that is how you dress for a funeral, sugar, your own, and I love that you planned ahead, it's the first sensible thing I've seen you do.", "Look at you, all dapper and doomed, and I can't decide if I want to read your future or just tell you it's pretty and take your money.", "You clean up nice, sugar, so please try not to bleed on it, because I can sell you a charm for luck but nothing in this shop gets out bloodstains.", "If you die in that suit, it'll at least be an open casket with taste, and I'll light a candle that I'll bill you for in advance."],
		"died": ["You died again, sugar, and I'll admit it's becoming a hobby, a bad one, but at least it's consistent, and I respect a man who commits to a bit.", "Oh, I saw it happen, honey, the whole floor did, and the cat that lives in my shop took one look and left the building without even asking for a refund.", "Dust yourself off, sugar. You woke up at home owing more than before, so go get your brother, and make that debt mean something.", "That was a bold way to lose, sugar, not smart, mind you, just bold, and in this town we put bold on the headstone and smart in the footnotes."],
		"boss": ["You beat a boss, sugar, and I want you to know I'll remember that fondly, right up until you owe me money, which will be in about three minutes.", "Impressive, sugar. Another casino boss dethroned, and now I'm wondering if I should be nicer to you, but then I remember my prices, and no.", "Another table won, and I hear the people who ran it had friends, mean wealthy friends, who will now be shopping for my most expensive curses.", "Sit, sugar, let me price that victory, because to you it's a triumph, but to me it's a market opportunity with excellent upsell potential."],
		"idle": ["I keep telling the cards to stop gossiping about you, sugar, but they love a good story, especially one that ends with someone losing everything.", "Everybody has a tell, Rico, and yours is hope, which is why I'll never stop selling it to you, it's like a leak that pays me.", "Charms, curses, and a little cold reading, sugar, that's the whole business, and the cold reading is mostly just me watching you lose.", "I'll let you in on a secret, sugar, nobody who buys a lucky charm ever stops needing one, and that's what we in the industry call retention."],
		"buy": ["Wise choice, sugar, or a terrible one, and you'll find out which, but the fee is the same either way, so I'm thrilled for both of us.", "Take it, it likes you, it likes everyone, it's a charm, that's the job, and attention-seeking is what I look for when I hire them.", "That charm bites a little, sugar, in a good way, mostly, and in the unlikely event it doesn't, I'll gladly sell you another one.", "Pleasure doing business, sugar, and I mean it, it was a pleasure for me, and for you it was an educational experience."]},
	"fizz": {
		"greet": ["Psst, over here, welcome to the pharmacy, which is not technically licensed, but I am required by law to tell you that and then immediately ask you to forget I did.", "Come closer, closer, not that close, ugh, you breathe a lot, anyway my products may cause drowsiness, euphoria, or in rare cases, a brief but meaningful friendship with a paramedic.", "Welcome to Doc Fizz's, where every bottle comes with a legally mandated warning, and today's warning is, please do not ask what the other bottle is for.", "A customer! Or a cop. Are you a cop? If you're a cop, this is a bakery, and these are very strong muffins."],
		"farewell": ["Side effects begin immediately, last permanently, and in rare cases, develop a French accent, which I'm legally required to say is not covered by my warranty.", "Go on, be amazing, or dead, statistically speaking, I should mention, it's mostly dead, but the ones who are amazing are really amazing.", "Take the bottle, keep the bottle, do not return the bottle, it's looking at me and I'd prefer not to discuss what it said.", "Don't tell anyone where you got that, especially me, because I've already forgotten, and legally I never met you."],
		"rich": ["Oh, you're loaded, so let me show you the good stuff, which is in the other bag, the one that hums, and which carries a warning I'm not allowed to read out loud.", "Cash, real cash, my favorite flavor, it tastes like a lawyer and it comes with a lawyer, and by law I must disclose that the lawyer is also in the product.", "For you, double price, triple effect, and quadruple the side effects, which now include, and I quote the form, a sudden desire to spend more money here.", "Hide that money inside my product, it's the safest place, except for the fact that my product is a liquid, and so is the money, after the first dose."],
		"broke": ["You're out of cash? I accept organs, small ones, spares really, you've got spares, right, because the form specifically says spares, and I'm legally required to ask.", "No money? Free sample, which is free as in, my liability is now your liability, and by taking it you agree to be liable for my feelings.", "I'll put it on your tab, Rico, and by tab I mean I'll bill your family, you have a family, right, because I just invented one for you, and I'm very strict.", "Come back when you've been mugged by someone richer than you, that way the muggers have standards and your wallet gets a better class of trauma."],
		"ugly": ["That outfit is already a hallucination, and I haven't even sold you anything, which is a first, and a legal concern, because who is responsible for that.", "You look like a warning label, Rico, which is flattering, because I love warning labels, I write them, they get worse every year, mine are eight pages now.", "Don't worry about the outfit, the drugs make everything look better, even me, and I've been told, by a bottle, that I'm very handsome in the right dose.", "I've seen better-fitting clothes on a cadaver, and in fairness, that cadaver was in the middle of a legal dispute, and had better lawyers."],
		"sharp": ["Fancy! That suit is going to look amazing right up until the moment you spill something on it, and my product spills in six different colors.", "Look at you, a well-dressed mistake, my absolute favorite kind of customer, because well-dressed mistakes always pay in cash and never read the label.", "You're too nice for this stall, Rico, so buy something and get less nice, side effects include a lowered moral baseline and an increased appetite for shrimp.", "Sharp! Let's ruin it with science, the side effects include stains, glowing, and a mild but persistent urge to join a cult."],
		"died": ["You look dead, which is wonderful, because it means my product works, though I'm required to say that I have no data supporting that, other than your face.", "I heard the scream, and it was you, and honestly, nice lungs, they carry very well, and I mean that as a legitimate compliment from a medical professional, sort of.", "Death isn't so bad, Rico, it's the respawn that's the real side effect, it's long, it's repetitive, and I'm told the loading screen is borderline unbearable.", "Please don't die near the merchandise, the insurance covers nothing, and I mean literally nothing, I checked, the policy is just a drawing of a duck."],
		"boss": ["You beat a boss! Give me your blood for science, just a pint, okay a gallon, and I'm legally obligated to say that it's not for science.", "You killed someone important, so celebrate with the red bottle, which is made from the previous boss's leftovers, and I should disclose that the label says do not.", "Bosses are just customers who never learned to share, and this one never paid his tab, so now I take payment in trophies, and a little in organs.", "Did he have a pulse, a tooth, a kidney? Asking for business reasons, not for my business, but for a second business that I'm required to deny exists."],
		"idle": ["I have a bottle that sings, but it's a terrible singer, mostly it screams, and by law I'm required to say that screaming is a known side effect of the bottle.", "Everything has side effects, even oxygen, ask anyone who's died of it, and that's why my labels are now sixteen pages, and the last four are just apologies.", "Don't read the label, Rico, the label is lying, and the label is also a bit of a coward, and the label is a cousin of mine, which I'm required to disclose.", "Tell me your symptoms, then ignore my advice, that's the whole medical process here, and it has a ninety percent success rate, in the sense that you keep coming back."],
		"buy": ["Drink it fast, no, slow, wait, fast, whichever one you didn't do, and by law I'm required to say that I forgot which one is safe, but they're both a gamble.", "Side effects include luck, liver failure, a brief conversation with God, and a strong opinion about jazz, and God is a big fan of yours, actually.", "Do not mix with alcohol, other medications, or the afternoon, and if you do mix it, please do it somewhere away from my shop, and my reputation, and my dog.", "A good choice, probably, I don't read, I just pour and pray, and the prayer is also legally required to say it's not responsible for the results."]},
	"tailor": {
		"greet": ["Do come in, but mind the pins, and the mannequins, they bite when ignored, and frankly you look like someone who ignores things, including mirrors.", "Ah, a customer, or a stray, hold still while I find out which, and please don't breathe on the silk, it's older than your last three decisions combined.", "Silas Stitch, at your service, and at your waistline, good heavens, there's a lot of it, we shall need the long measuring tape, and possibly a second tailor.", "Welcome, welcome, and please sit before you offend the mannequins, they have feelings, and sadly they have extremely strong opinions about what you've chosen to wear today."],
		"farewell": ["Wear it well, Rico, or at least wear it, please do not carry it, and under no circumstances should you ever put it in a fanny pack.", "Mind the hem on your way out, and the door, and your life choices, though I fear only one of those will ever be fixed by a tailor.", "Do try not to bleed on the silk, or the wool, or me, I only have the one handkerchief and it's a rental.", "Come back for a fitting, and a lecture, I've prepared the lecture, it's forty minutes, and it begins with your shoes, and ends with your mother."],
		"rich": ["Splendid, a gentleman with means, which means we can finally begin the long and lovely lie that you have taste, starting with a very expensive belt.", "Ah, the pockets are heavy, which means the hems shall be lovely, and I'll bill you for both, and for the sheer emotional labor of looking at you.", "With that fortune, we might finally fix your posture, though I suspect surgery is the only honest option, and it's a lovely table, I've seen it.", "Money, how delightfully vulgar, please, spend it on me, beautifully, and I'll make you a coat so fine that the House itself will ask for the name of your tailor."],
		"broke": ["No funds? Then we tailor in imagination, Rico, imagine a very nice belt, there, that's two dollars, and imagining the pants is another ten.", "I can offer you a very nice belt of regret, it's free, it's itchy, and it clashes with literally everything, including your skin.", "Poverty is merely fashion in beta, darling, and you've been in beta for years, and the reviews, I'm afraid, have been devastating.", "Come back when you can afford sleeves, my dear, until then you are a vest, and frankly, a tragic one, but at least a well-ventilated one."],
		"ugly": ["Dear boy, did you dress yourself in a dumpster, don't answer, the smell has already answered, and it said it needs a moment alone with the mannequins.", "That fanny pack is a war crime, and I'd gladly testify, in my best suit, which is the one thing in this room not currently offended by you.", "I will not say what I think, I will faint, watch, there, I'm back up, and I'll need a moment, and possibly a glass of water and a different customer.", "You look like a rumor of an outfit, Rico, and a poorly sourced rumor at that, and even my mannequins have turned to face the wall."],
		"sharp": ["Now that is a proper silhouette, Rico, a murder suspect, but a dapper one, and I'd gladly be your character witness for the tailoring alone.", "Magnificent, I'd put it in a museum, right next to the exhibit of men who died wearing it, which is, I'm told, a very popular wing.", "You are a credit to the craft, Rico, and to my commission, and in a rare moment of sincerity, I might even stop judging your shoes.", "I made half of that outfit, and the other half is you, barely, squint, and it almost works, and I am prepared to take all the credit."],
		"died": ["You died in my wares, Rico? Did it stain? Please say it didn't stain, because I can fix a hole, but I cannot fix a blood type.", "A dead client is a quiet client, which I love, but a bloody client is a lawsuit, and my lawyer is a mannequin, and she is not good.", "Do bleed on the old stock, if you must, but never on the new silk, never the silk, I had a long conversation with that silk and I promised it a better life.", "Hold still, I'll repair the holes, and which of these are bullet holes and which are style, don't tell me, I'd rather imagine they're all the second thing."],
		"boss": ["Defeated a boss, how marvelous, then you'll need armor, fashionable armor, because is there any other kind, and I assure you the answer is no.", "Slaying monsters in silk, how delightful, and for the record, stains come out with lemon, wine, and prayer, in that order, and the prayer is mostly for me.", "The trophies will need a tasteful frame, Rico, and a priest, and possibly a slightly better class of enemy, one who dresses with some intention.", "I once made that boss a custom suit, and he hated it, and now he's dead, so in a way, it's a little better, and I take full credit."],
		"idle": ["Gloves for gripping, boots for smashing, scarves for gliding, and hats for nothing, I just like hats, and I'm not required to defend that.", "The shoes make the man, the man makes the dash, and the dash makes my rent, and honestly I'd prefer the man to hold still for a fitting.", "Stand straight, Rico, the cloth knows, and the cloth is judging your spine, and the cloth is, I'm sorry to say, extremely disappointed.", "Everything I sell grants a talent, mostly vanity, occasionally a double jump, and I've never been able to tell which of those is more useful in this building."],
		"buy": ["A fine choice, I knew it would suit you, and I say that to everyone, and it's never true, but this time I'd like to think it's slightly less false.", "Wear it with confidence, Rico, or at the very least with shoes, because shoes are the minimum, and I'm still not convinced you own any.", "I shall tell the thread you said hello, and the thread has opinions, and they involve you, and none of them are flattering, and I'm going to relay all of them.", "One moment while I finish, the pins are my pride, and also my weapons, and I do not want to discuss the second thing with the authorities."]},
	"gunny": {
		"greet": ["Welcome to the armory, recruit, and please say hello to Betsy, she's the one on the left, she's seen things, and I think she likes you, which is a first.", "Stand up straight, recruit, you're in the presence of firepower, and I'm not talking about me, I'm talking about the lovely lady on the wall, and I'm blushing.", "Rack em and stack em, gamblers, we've got everything that goes bang, and nothing that goes whimper, and that second category is where you come in.", "You need firepower, I can smell it on you, and a shower, I can smell that too, but one of those I can fix with a very large shotgun."],
		"farewell": ["Don't shoot your foot, recruit, shoot theirs, it's a different foot, and Betsy would be so disappointed if you mixed those up, and so would I.", "Dismissed, and try to die forward, because dying backward is how you lose the deposit, and Betsy hates paperwork.", "Clean your guns, wash your hands, but never your lucky socks, they're load-bearing, and I won't have you ruin a perfectly good superstition.", "Move out, rookie, and don't bet the ammo, I know you, I KNOW you, and I've already named the bullets after the ones you're going to lose."],
		"rich": ["Cash! The universal caliber! You walk in here with that kind of money, and Betsy just started purring, I swear to you, it's the first time since the divorce.", "A big spender! I salute your wallet, and the gorgeous weight of it, and if I could marry it, I'd have to ask Betsy first, and she's very protective.", "Now that is purchasing power, recruit, and I'll throw in a free ammo clip, a salute, and a very long moment alone with the new shotgun, if you don't mind.", "With that kind of money, I'll show you the good stuff, but you have to promise to treat her right, because she's my daughter, in a very specific, legally unclear way."],
		"broke": ["No money, no bang, recruit, it's simple, it's the oldest rule in the armory, and it's also pretty much the plot of your whole life.", "Broke? Throw rocks, they're a classic, and rocks have a perfect safety record, mostly, if you ignore the last one, which I'm told was a glacier.", "A recruit with no cash, huh, that's a start, and also a funeral, and I'd just like to say, Betsy and I will be sending flowers.", "I'm not a charity, recruit, I'm a battle store, and the difference is the screaming, and mostly it's Betsy, who hates it when you touch the shelves."],
		"ugly": ["Soldier, that outfit is a disciplinary action, and a war crime, and a Tuesday, and I've seen less offensive things come out of a mortar.", "Camouflage? You look like a bruise, a sad wandering bruise, and the thing is, Betsy just looked at you and sighed, and she never sighs.", "I've seen better uniforms on a scarecrow, recruit, and the scarecrow had a better stance, and a stronger sense of purpose, and frankly a nicer rifle.", "What happened to your pants, recruit, did the House take them, and did they give them back, because if they did, I'd like to speak to them about a recall."],
		"sharp": ["Spit-shined, recruit, I'm almost proud, I'm even a little emotional, but we are not discussing that, and the shotgun in the corner is not a witness.", "That suit says I'm lethal in four languages, and it's a shame you only speak panic, but Betsy likes it, and she's an excellent judge of character.", "You look like a general, recruit, so behave like one, which means sending others to die first, and keeping the good guns for yourself, as God and I intended.", "A sharp dresser holds a gun better, it's a scientific fact, I've measured it, and the guns agree, they find you more attractive, which is frankly unsettling."],
		"died": ["You're dead? Walk it off, recruit, or crawl it off, either way, just get it off, because you're bleeding on Betsy, and she just had her stock polished.", "That's what armor is for, recruit, and you forgot your armor, you always forget your armor, and I always hand you a new one, like a patient father.", "Retrain, rearm, resurrect, repeat, that's the entire military, and also your whole career, and Betsy would like it noted that she's proud of the effort.", "The only bad death is the unarmed one, and I regret to inform you, recruit, yours was exactly that kind, and Betsy would like a word about it."],
		"boss": ["A boss, defeated, recruit, medals for everyone except the boss, who gets a closed casket, and Betsy gets a new coat of oil, because she earned it.", "That's the kind of firepower I like, large, loud, and legally ambiguous, and I'm told it's the same thing my ex-wife said about me, and I took it as a compliment.", "I sold that boss his first revolver, and I regret nothing, except his trigger discipline, which was, I'm sorry to say, a personal failure of mine.", "You make me proud, recruit, and don't make it weird, and it's too late, it's weird, and Betsy is looking at me, and I'm taking a moment."],
		"idle": ["I've been thinking about naming the new shotgun, and I want your honest opinion, and it's either Marjorie or Danielle, and she's very sensitive, so choose carefully.", "A revolver has six reasons, recruit, use five, save one for the barista, and I won't say which barista, but he knows what he did.", "The coin shotgun is my favorite, don't ask why, it's illegal in four countries and a Pizza Hut, and I miss that Pizza Hut every single day.", "Weapons don't kill people, bad odds do, and pointy things, and Gary, and I will not be taking questions about Gary, and Betsy will not be taking questions about Gary."],
		"buy": ["Excellent choice, recruit, now point it away from yourself, and me, and the cat, and also Betsy, she's sensitive about being aimed at.", "That's a classic, recruit, so respect it, it's seen things, mostly foreheads, and it has a way of looking at you, like a very polite old soldier.", "Eight out of ten customers survive their first purchase, and you, recruit, are a nine, which I'm told is a mathematical impossibility, and Betsy agrees.", "Good choice, recruit, and be gentle with her, she kicks, mostly the person holding her, so hold her tighter, and if she makes a sound, that's just the love."]},
	"lucky": {
		"greet": ["Pull up a stool, runner, and mind the one with the stain, it's fond of you, and by fond I mean it's currently winning me forty dollars in a pool about where you'll die.", "The usual? Whatever that was, you never finish your sentences, mostly because the last time you did, you were dying, and I had a lot riding on the sentence.", "Lucky's, where we don't water it much, and we definitely don't change the ice, and the pool on how you're going to die is currently up to six hundred.", "Good to see you breathing, runner, I had you at even money for not, and I lost, and I've never been happier to lose, but don't tell the guys in the pool."],
		"farewell": ["Drink responsibly, or at least drink first, that's the whole policy, and I'll keep a stool warm for you, and a pool open on how you leave this one.", "Come back in one piece, or two pieces, I'm not picky, I have a mop, and a very serious bet on which one it'll be, and I'm hoping for three.", "I'll keep your seat warm and your tab open, it's the only thing around here that never closes, and also I have the pool, which closes at midnight.", "Break a leg, runner, but not your own, someone else's, it's nicer, and also I've got twenty bucks on the leg, so please be specific."],
		"rich": ["First round's on me, second on you, and the third on your fortune, and your remaining dignity, and also, runner, the pool just changed, and everybody's betting you lose it all by dinner.", "That's a lot of green, runner, so I've got a Scotch that'll cry, a good cry, and I've got six guys in the pool who'd cry harder if you kept it.", "Cash like that needs a toast and an alibi, and I can provide the toast, and one of the pool guys can provide the alibi, for a modest fee.", "You're buying, aren't you, runner, it's not a question, I'm already getting the glasses, and I've updated the pool to say you died drunk and rich."],
		"broke": ["Tab's on me tonight, runner, but don't make it a habit, make it a hobby, a small one, and the pool is now offering you a ten percent cut if you die before closing.", "I'll pour you water, runner, it's all I've got that's free, and it's also all I've got that's honest, and I'm not even sure about the honesty.", "Broke? Join the club, I'm the president, and the dues are one drink per sorrow, and the pool has moved your death odds to the front of the board.", "Not a problem, runner, sit, cry, hydrate, the tears are on the house, and the guys in the pool are already betting on how long you last without a drink."],
		"ugly": ["That outfit's strong, runner, like my worst whiskey, and you smell about the same, and I've got a pool going on which one of you wins.", "Not my business what you wear, runner, but it's very much my business that it hurts, and I've moved the pool to include death by fashion.", "I've seen better coats in the lost and found, runner, and the coats were also on fire, and still more flattering than whatever that is.", "A drink might help, runner, or at least blur it, for both of us, and the pool is up to nine hundred dollars on whether you notice."],
		"sharp": ["Look at you, runner, all class and no chaser, wait, I have chasers, oh good, and the pool now has a category for best dressed corpse, and you're the front-runner.", "Dressed to kill, or at least be killed in, runner, and it's a good look either way, and I've got forty dollars on the second one.", "That suit deserves a good Scotch, runner, and you deserve a cheap one, fair, and I've taken the liberty of adding it to the pool.", "You almost look like you belong here, runner, but don't worry, one drink will fix that, and two will make the pool really interesting."],
		"died": ["Welcome back, runner, I had you dying on the stairs, so honestly, thank you, and drinks are on the guy who bet on spikes, he's very upset.", "Rough one, runner, I had you picked for the elevator, so now I owe a man in a hat forty bucks, and he's very smug, and I'd like you to take that personally.", "Ah, you died, runner, so have a drink, it doesn't help, but it's something to do with your hands, and also the pool just paid out, so it's on me.", "A drink can save your life, runner, a second can end it, and a third is the Marker, and I've got the receipts on all three."],
		"boss": ["You beat a boss, runner? Next round's on me, and the one after, and the funeral, because I had you dying to him, and I've got to pay the other side.", "Cheers to the one that fell, runner, may he rest, and may his tab be forgiven, it won't be, and the pool paid out ten to one on you, so I'm on the hook.", "That boss drank here, runner, and he tipped badly, and he died worse, and I had him at forty to one, so thank you for the loss.", "A toast to the one who didn't die tonight, runner, tonight being relative, and I've already put money on tomorrow."],
		"idle": ["I keep a bar on most floors, runner, out of spite and grief, mostly grief, and the spite is a bonus, and the grief is mostly yours.", "I've got a pool going on how many times you'll die before you reach the Bellagiro, and the current number is fifty-three, and the guy with the number sixty is crying.", "A drink never lies, runner, only the drinker does, and the bartender, and don't ask me about the bartender, because he's me, and I have a pool on that too.", "My whole job is wiping a glass and listening, runner, and apologizing, and honestly, nine times out of ten the apology is for the pool."],
		"buy": ["Bottoms up, runner, and gently, like a bad idea, and I've put a small bet on how long that lasts, and my odds are not in your favor.", "That one has a kick, runner, and a story, and neither has an ending, and I've got a pool on both of them.", "Careful, runner, don't spill your luck, spill your guts, it's different, and I'll bet you ten bucks that you do both.", "On the house, runner, sort of, I mean the House won't cover it, it never does, but the pool will, and the pool loves you."]},
	"mags": {
		"greet": ["Rico, sweetheart, my favorite investment, you look absolutely terrible, which is wonderful news for my interest rate, and I'm so glad you came, I was starting to miss the debt.", "I was just counting your debt, kid, and it's so big now, it's grown so much, and I swear it has your eyes, and I've decided to keep it as a pet.", "Sit, sit, sit, standing is fine too, for now, I'm lenient on the first visit, and I only bite on the second, and by bite I mean charge you.", "Kid, you're on time, I love that, I hate late, late is where the bodies are, and your debt is very much alive, so we'll get along."],
		"farewell": ["Don't make me swim after you, Rico, I just did my hair, well, the scalp, and I'd hate to get it wet, but I will, sweetie, I will.", "I'll see you soon, kid, you'll see me sooner, that's just physics, and my debt to you is basically a love letter, and I'm writing back.", "Pay me, sweetie, or I'll collect, and I say that with so much love, I really do, and a little with teeth.", "Be careful out there, kid, it would be such a waste, of my time, I mean, and a bit of my heart, but mostly my time."],
		"rich": ["Look at all that money, Rico, it looks so lonely, so let me adopt it, I have room, and a very large tank, and the tank is the only thing I'm going to say about it.", "A big pot, sweetheart, and a bigger interest, and a biggest me, and I'd love to borrow a little, the way a shark borrows a swimmer.", "You can pay me early, kid, you won't, but you can, and that's the spirit I adore in you, which is to say none at all.", "Money, my favorite snack, Rico, and it tastes like retirement, and I'd like you to hold it for me, just for a moment, near my mouth."],
		"broke": ["Broke, sweetie? I'll float you, a shark takes care of its fish, briefly, and then, dinner, and I can't wait for you to see how well I cook.", "Empty pockets, kid, and so much potential, mine, and I love the way you tremble when I say that.", "I never judge, Rico, I just remember, every dollar, every missed call, every pet name, and I've named your debt Buttons.", "A loan keeps the family together, sweetheart, mine, yours is optional, and I'll always be here, like a nice warm mortgage."],
		"ugly": ["That outfit is a loan officer's nightmare, Rico, and I want it framed, so I can look at it when I need to feel better about my own life choices.", "Oh sweetie, I'd lend you a suit, interest only, forever, but look at the cuffs, they're already forever, and so, I'm afraid, are you.", "Is that a fanny pack, Rico? I'm calling your mother, I'm calling all your mothers, and I'm bringing the debt, so she can meet him.", "I've collected from better-dressed corpses, kid, not by much, they were better-dressed by a lot, and one of them had a very lovely tie."],
		"sharp": ["Nice suit, kid, it looks expensive, and I know whose, it's mine, you're wearing my money, and honestly, it fits you better than it fit me.", "Dressed to impress, sweetheart, and I'm impressed, now pay up, and I'll let you keep the cufflinks, as a gesture of my love.", "That's a lot of my money on your back, Rico, so I'll take a cut, of the back, and I'll start with the shoulders.", "Now you look like a lender, kid, good news, you're not, and better news, neither am I, I'm a relationship."],
		"died": ["You died, sweetie, and I'm adding it to your interest, because death is a surcharge, and I think of it as a little gift to myself.", "No refunds in the afterlife, Rico, I'd know, I've got a branch there, and it's got the best view, and it's staffed by your debt.", "Dead men don't pay, kid, but they do borrow, I've seen it, it's a whole thing, and it's one of my best markets.", "Death is just a late payment, sweetheart, of a different sort, and both lead to me, and I'll be waiting with a pen."],
		"boss": ["A boss, defeated, kid? Their debt belongs to me now, and their dog, I don't want the dog, but you'll bring it to me, and I'll pretend to be surprised.", "Take your spoils, Rico, I'll take my share, we call it a share, the law calls it something else, and honestly the law is jealous.", "Winning's expensive, sweetheart, so let me carry it, in my teeth, and I promise I'll bring you back a nice receipt.", "You beat the boss, kid, now beat the interest, good luck, nobody has, not even me, and I made the interest."],
		"idle": ["Don't think of it as debt, sweetie, think of it as a relationship, a deep one, with teeth, and I promise I'll be gentle, mostly with the paperwork.", "I like you, Rico, and that's the problem, because I like everything I eat, and you're looking particularly delicious today.", "Everybody owes somebody, kid, I just own the paperwork, and the walls, and the floor, and a little bit of your left kidney.", "I swim every day, sweetheart, just in case, and the case is you, and I'm very, very prepared."],
		"buy": ["Sign here, and here, and there, and don't read it, kid, nobody reads it, nobody lives, and I find that so romantic.", "A pleasure, Rico, I'll bill you later, and later, and now, actually, now I billed you, and it's so wonderful to have you as a customer.", "Smart, kid, debt is just future money you spent early, think of it as time travel with teeth, and my teeth are very large.", "No refunds, sweetheart, no regrets, some regrets, almost all regrets, and they're all yours, and I'll hold them for you, gently."]},
	"marlow": {
		"greet": ["Rico, you picked up, good, I had a bet with myself that you'd die before the second ring, and I lost, and I'm so relieved I may cry into my sandwich.", "Marlow here, talk fast, the line's got ears, and mold, mostly mold, and I'm eating a very sad sandwich, so I'm in no mood for surprises.", "Back already, kid? I was just worrying, constructively, with snacks, and honestly it's the closest thing I have to a hobby, besides regret.", "Hey, are you alive, say something stupid, there, alive, and I'll stop checking, but I'll keep guilt-checking, which I do every hour."],
		"farewell": ["Stay alive, stay lucky, stay on the line, pick any two, never three, and I say this as a man who got your brother his seat at the table.", "Call me if you need me, kid, call me if you don't, I'm lonely, that's classified, and I'll be here, with my guilt, and a snack.", "Don't do anything I'd worry about, Rico, too late, I'm already composing the eulogy, and it begins with a sandwich, which makes me look good.", "Let it ride, kid, preferably into a wall that's padded, and give my regards to your brother, the one I got the seat for, ugh, I hate saying that."],
		"rich": ["Look at that pot, Rico, resist the urge, resist it, resist it, you didn't resist it, and now I'm eating a second sandwich, out of stress.", "You're rich, kid, don't tell the House, don't tell yourself either, and for the love of everything, don't tell Jules, because he'll want to borrow it.", "Bank it, Rico, please, bank it, I'm begging, I'm on the floor, that's a dust bunny, and I'm on a first-name basis with it.", "I've seen guys lose that in one hand, kid, and I've also been one of them, and Jules was in the room, and I'd rather not talk about it."],
		"broke": ["Broke again, kid? That's the third time today, and it's lunch, and I'm starting to think your brother is a better planner, which is deeply upsetting.", "Hey, it's just money, Rico, it comes back, mostly, maybe, look, it's a hope, not a promise, and I'm a bad promise guy, ask Jules.", "I'll cover dinner, kid, just don't tell your brother, he still thinks I'm solvent, and I'd like to keep that illusion alive, along with my guilt.", "You're not broke, Rico, you're liquid, in a sad way, like a puddle, and I've been told I give the same energy, but with a sandwich."],
		"ugly": ["Rico, what are you wearing, I can hear it, it's whispering help, and I'm on a payphone, which means I'm the one who's actually suffering.", "Is that a fanny pack, kid, on the phone, I can see it, don't ask how, and I'm so sorry, I hang up on people for less.", "Look, style isn't everything, Rico, it's most things, it's like eighty percent, and I've gotten through life on the other twenty, which is why I'm on a payphone.", "Please, kid, go see Silas, for my sake, I can't unsee it, and I'm on a payphone, and I've got no window to look out of, just guilt."],
		"sharp": ["Hey, nice suit, kid, I can hear the starch, it's screaming don't bleed, and I second that, because I owe a lot of favors on that fabric.", "You look like a man with a plan, Rico, do you have a plan, blink twice if no, you can't blink, it's a phone, and now I'm even more worried.", "Dressed to kill, kid, try not to be killed, it's a fine line, and your tailor knows it, and so does your brother, who I'm still apologizing to.", "Nice threads, Rico, don't get blood on them, I called in a lot of favors for those, and I'd hate to have to explain to a mannequin."],
		"died": ["Rico, again? We have to stop meeting like this, in a morgue, via payphone, and I'm eating my feelings, which, unfortunately, are a tuna salad.", "I heard the thud, kid, it was a loud one, I clapped, don't judge me, and then I felt terrible, and then I ate a second sandwich.", "You died, Rico, so I'll light a candle, a small one, a very small one, it's a matchstick, and it's also a reminder that I got Jules his seat.", "Good news, kid, you're alive, bad news, it's me and the phone, and Jules is still missing, and I'm still the guy who got him the seat."],
		"boss": ["A boss, defeated, Rico? I'm updating my bet, and I'm betting you survive, which is a first, and I'm going to put it in writing, so you can't back out.", "That's one more casino beaten, kid, Jules is a little closer, or a little farther, I'm still checking the map, and by map I mean a napkin.", "You did it, Rico, don't let it go to your head, let it go to your knees, then bank it, and I'll have a sandwich ready.", "I'm proud of you, kid, and I hate that, I'm checking my pulse, and also my conscience, which, to be fair, is the same thing."],
		"idle": ["Five casinos, kid, twenty-five floors, and Jules at the top of the Bellagiro, easy, by which I mean impossible, in that order, and I'm so, so sorry.", "I keep thinking about the day I got Jules that seat at the table, Rico, and I keep thinking it was a favor, and I keep eating, which doesn't help.", "Follow the light, kid, it leads somewhere, hopefully not a morgue, and if it does, call me, and I'll pick up, because I'm the guy who picks up.", "Every floor has a story, Rico, some bleed, most are about you losing, and mine is about me, and a payphone, and a sandwich, and a very bad decision."],
		"buy": ["Good call, kid, not great, good, like good on a report card for a goldfish, and I'm eating a sandwich in celebration, a small one.", "I hope you read the fine print, Rico, there's no fine print, that's the fine print, and I should know, I've signed everything, including your brother's seat.", "I wouldn't, kid, but I'm not you, thank God, thank all the gods, and I'm saying that with guilt, and a little bit of mayo.", "That's the one Jules would have bought, Rico, and look where that got him, and by that I mean, look where it got me, because I'm the one who feels bad."]},
	"jules": {
		"greet": ["Rico, is it really you? I've had that hallucination before, and he's usually taller, and he usually has a sandwich, and I'm just saying, one more hand, and I'll be right with you.", "I knew you'd come, Rico, I just didn't know when, I did bet on never, but I'm winning, so that's fine, I'm definitely winning, just give me one more hand.", "One more hand, just one, oh, it's you, you can have the hand, I'm winning anyway, I'm up by, I don't want to say the number, because it's a lot.", "Is it morning, Rico, what day is it, is there a day, who has the clock, and more importantly, one more hand, and I'll tell you all about it."],
		"farewell": ["Don't wait for me, Rico, go, I'm busy, I'm winning, I'm basically a legend, I just need one more hand, and then I'll be right out, probably.", "Say hi to Mom, or don't, she'll worry, and then she'll ask for the money back, and I'll say I'm winning, and she'll say that's what you said last time.", "Take the money, leave the cards, and the dice, and the chair, I'm attached to the chair, and also I'm winning, and I'll be here when you come back.", "Come back, I'll be here, I'm always here, it's a whole problem, and also, one more hand, I swear, then I'm done."],
		"rich": ["That's a lot of chips, Rico, I know the feeling, don't trust it, it's a lie told by a sparkly liar, and I'm winning, by the way, just in case you're wondering.", "I had that much once, for ten minutes, and then I had a dealer's smile, and I'm still up, in a way, and one more hand will prove it.", "Bank it, Rico, I'm begging, I'm not above begging, I'm lower than it, watch, and also I'm winning, so I don't need the help.", "I was rich once, Rico, it didn't help, it just changed how I lost, and I'm winning now, and the winning feels so, so different."],
		"broke": ["Broke, Rico? Welcome, it's cozy, the walls are close, and the rent is nothing, and I'm winning, so I'm only in here for the ambience.", "I've been broke for three years, Rico, it's fine, I have a lot of hobbies, mostly regret, and also winning, I'm very, very winning.", "It's just money, Rico, it was never ours, it was the House's, look at the logo, and I'm winning it back, one hand at a time.", "At least we're broke together, Rico, that's called family, or a pyramid scheme, and I'm winning, so I'll let you buy in at a discount."],
		"ugly": ["Nice outfit, Rico, I love it, I'm lying, I'm so lying, and I'm winning, so I can afford to be honest, and it's a crime.", "I'd say something, Rico, but you're my brother, I'd just say it more quietly, and I'm winning, so I'll let it slide.", "You look like me after three years, Rico, and one stain, is that mine, and I'm up, by the way, so don't worry about the stain.", "Mom would cry, Rico, then laugh, then ask where you got it, then cry again, and I'm winning, so I can afford to cry."],
		"sharp": ["You look great, Rico, suspiciously great, who died, is it me, is it me, and I'm winning, so it can't be me, can it?", "Look at you, Rico, Dad would be proud, Dad would also ask where you stole it, and I'm winning, so I'm proud too.", "I used to dress like that, Rico, before, now I dress like before, and I'm winning, so I can afford to dress like anything.", "Did you buy that with my debts, Rico, it's got my fingerprints, and my interest, and I'm winning, so I'll forgive you."],
		"died": ["You died, Rico, welcome to my life, it's less dead than you'd think, and more dead than I'd like, and I'm winning, so it's mostly fine.", "It doesn't hurt after the first twenty, Rico, then it's just administrative, and I'm winning, so I've got a lot of paperwork.", "I've died here a hundred times, Rico, you get used to it, and the lighting, and I'm winning, so it's fine, it's all fine.", "Get up, Rico, it's just money, and a body, and a soul, and a deposit, and I'm winning, so I'll cover the soul."],
		"boss": ["You beat a boss, Rico? I never got past the third, or did, they blur together, like all my mistakes, and I'm winning, so I'm taking credit.", "I heard the table go quiet, Rico, it was you, or the building collapsing, both are fine, and I'm winning, so I'll take either.", "The House is going to notice, Rico, it notices everything, it noticed me twice, and I'm winning, so I'm a little nervous.", "I'm proud, Rico, and scared, and a little jealous, mostly jealous, win more, loser, and I'm winning, so I'm a little jealous of myself."],
		"idle": ["The cards remember everything, Rico, especially the bad ones, especially me, and I'm winning, so they're basically my friends.", "You hear that, Rico, the wheel, it never stops, it also never says sorry, and I'm winning, so it's fine.", "I counted every floor, Rico, there's more, always more, it's a growing business, and I'm winning, so I'm one of the owners.", "Be careful with the House, Rico, it's not a person, it's a vibe with lawyers, and I'm winning, so I'm basically a lawyer."],
		"buy": ["Good pick, Rico, I'd have picked it too, I lost anyway, eventually, with style, and I'm winning, so ignore that.", "Take my advice, Rico, don't, take my advice again, don't, you're not listening, brother, and I'm winning, so listen anyway.", "It might work, Rico, mine didn't, but I'm an optimist, by which I mean broke, and also winning, mostly the first one.", "At least you're trying, Rico, that's what I said, right before the funeral, and I'm winning, so please take that as a good sign."]},
	"rico": {
		"greet": ["Let's see what the House has left me, besides my brother, my dignity, and a very small stack of chips that I'm calling a portfolio.", "Aces up, brains out, perfect, that's the whole strategy, and I'm told it's also how the House describes its customers.", "Another day, another dollar I don't have, and will never have, hey, at least it's consistent, and that's called momentum.", "Let it ride, baby, or let it flop, I'm indifferent, I'm lying, LET IT RIDE, and also I need a second opinion on my life."],
		"farewell": ["Wish me luck, not that I need it, I need it so much, please, and I'm saying that to a vending machine, but still.", "See you at the top of the Bellagiro, or at the bottom of a dumpster, same energy, and I'll bring Jules either way.", "I'll be rich by dinner, or dead, and honestly, both are on the menu, and the second one is a tasting menu.", "Let it ride, and if it doesn't, let it die, dramatically, with a really good last line, and a respawn timer."],
		"rich": ["I'm rich, wait, let me count again, I'm rich, wait, that's one chip, fine, still rich, and that's the House's fault for teaching me math.", "Look at all this, I'm going to bet it, all of it, it's the only responsible thing, and by responsible I mean exactly what you think.", "Money, that's just ammunition, and the House is armed with my debts, so we're basically in a very polite war.", "The pot's fat, so it's time to make it fatter, and then lose it, for balance, because the universe loves a good symmetry."],
		"broke": ["Broke, that's just a free roll, with a funeral, same thing, and I've never been so ready to be somebody's problem.", "Zero dollars, infinite possibilities, mostly bad ones, mostly involving a pawn shop, and I've already got a ring in mind, and it's Jules's.", "I've been broker, I'm fine, I'm fine, I'm fine, does this look fine, don't answer, because the answer is the House.", "Rock bottom has a nice view, of other, deeper bottoms, and I'm told the elevator there is always out of order."],
		"ugly": ["I look like a dumpster fire and I love it, because fire is warm, and dumpsters are home, and I'm starting to think this is my brand.", "Is this fanny pack lucky, it's lucky, it's lucky, please be lucky, I'm begging a fanny pack, which is a new low, even for me.", "Style is for people with odds, I have vibes, and a belt of regret, and I'm going to wear them both to the next boss fight.", "Somebody call a stylist, or a priest, or an exorcist, or a stylist who's also an exorcist, and I'll pay in future winnings."],
		"sharp": ["I look incredible, the House should be scared, the House should also be on a payment plan, and by House I mean me, and by scared I mean impressed.", "Dressed to kill, or at least to lose in style, and honestly, style is the only thing I keep, besides debt, and a brother I'm still chasing.", "Hey, I clean up nice, I mean it, just don't look at the shoes, the shoes are in debt, and the debt is in love with the shoes.", "Would you bet on me, I would, I do, I did, and that's the whole problem, and also the whole charm."],
		"died": ["Okay, that one was on me, the one before that was on a wall, fine, and the one before that was on a bet I really should have thought through.", "Death, barely noticed, I do it for a living, a bad one, a living-ish one, and the loading screen is starting to know my name.", "I'll do it differently next time, or exactly the same, because variety is overrated, and so is dignity, and so, frankly, is breathing.", "I regret nothing, except that, and the thing before, and the entire year, and I'm told that's a healthy attitude in this building."],
		"boss": ["Read em and weep, pal, you're weeping already, good, good for you, and I'll send flowers to your next of kin, who I assume is the House.", "Another table won, and another reason to gamble, I mean ANOTHER reason, the first was my entire personality, and the second is a dead boss.", "I called the bluff, and the bluff folded, and then it cried, which was unprofessional, but I respected the commitment.", "Who's next, don't answer, I don't want to know, okay, answer, but make it dramatic, and with good lighting."],
		"idle": ["Odds are for people who don't have a gun, or a plan, or a savings, and I'm happy to be the one guy with none of the above.", "I once bet my shoes, won, lost the shoes, same thing, zero net shoes, and I walked home barefoot, and on the way I won another bet.", "Risk is just fun with consequences, and a rash, mostly the rash, and I'm told the rash is the sign that it's working.", "Climb five casinos, get Jules, don't bet him, it's three steps, and I've only failed step three, in theory, which means I'm technically undefeated."],
		"buy": ["Take my money, take all of it, wait, not all of it, ah, fine, all of it, and I'll just assume the receipt is a poem.", "Sold, wait, what was the price, never mind, sold, sold, sold, and Jules would be so proud, which is exactly the problem.", "Worth it, probably, and if I die, it's a charitable donation to someone with fewer problems, which is, frankly, everybody.", "That's a terrible deal, I'm in, I'm so in, I'm already in the pool, and I'll be the guy who loses, again."]},
}
